; --- swing : the committing action, as a sprite-sheet frame clip ------------
; CHANGE-BRIEF.md §6's phase table, in frames at 30 fps:
;
;   startup   frames 0-5    0.000 - 0.200   cell 5, windup. Locked.
;   active    frames 6-9    0.200 - 0.333   cell 6, live. Hitbox is LIVE.
;   recovery  frames 10-17  0.333 - 0.600   settles back. Still locked.
;   end       frame 18      0.600           cell 1, idle. Movement returns.
;
; The body cells are p6-windup and p7-live, generated for walker-ninja in
; 2026-10 and never used until now. The startup and active poses are real
; art, not frames invented for this assignment.
[sub_resource type="Animation" id="Animation_swing"]
